    "answer": {
      "short": "$(-\\infty,-5)\\cup(2,\\infty)$.",
      "worked": "Let $y=f(x)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{1-3x}{2}\\\\3x&=1-2y\\\\|3x-4|&=|1-2y-4|\\\\|3x-4|&=|2y+3|\\end{align*}$$\nThe domain restriction becomes $|2y+3|>7$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2y+3&<-7\\quad\\text{or}\\quad 2y+3>7\\\\y&<-5\\quad\\text{or}\\quad y>2\\end{align*}$$\nThe range is $(-\\infty,-5)\\cup(2,\\infty)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
